# GPT-6.2 Astra — findings by Step 5 Preview (self-excluded: model not officially released — zero verified public benchmarks)

- Source: OpenAI (`gpt-6.2-astra` — reported model ID, unconfirmed)
- Date: 2026-11-13 (UTC)
- Overview and scoring methodology: `../../model-comparison.md`
- Cross-model signed log: `../../model-findings.md`

## Model card

- **Name:** GPT-6.2 Astra (reported name/ID; never announced by OpenAI)
- **Short description:** An unreleased OpenAI model that surfaced only as a label in Codex usage analytics, Google Cloud quota screenshots and X posts between Nov 1–10, 2026 — no announcement, no API availability, no specs, no benchmarks.
- **Provider / access:** None verified. `gpt-6.2-astra` does not appear in OpenAI's public model catalog, API changelog, or pricing as of 2026-11-13 (checked directly). OpenAI's flagship catalog today lists GPT-6 Astra, GPT-6.1 Sol, GPT-6.1 Terra and GPT-6 Luna only.
- **Release / knowledge:** No release. Evidence trail: Codex usage-analytics screenshots (Oct 31 bar only, shares from 1.6% to 37.7% per account), a reused JSON fragment showing `response.model: gpt-6.2-astra`, Google Cloud quota-page screenshots (`base_model:gpt-6.2-astra`, `base_model:gpt-6.2-sol`) that later disappeared, and a terminal screenshot reading `gpt-6.2-astra xhigh`. Altman said on Nov 2 (ADIPEC) that the next GPT — the model behind the Navier–Stokes multi-agent run — is "coming soon"; The Information reported a possible Nov 6 launch of new Astra/Sol/Cyber versions; neither materialized. A Nov 10 docs reference to "models 6.2 and later" was removed the same day.
- **IDs:** `gpt-6.2-astra` (unconfirmed label only; not callable). Confirmed sibling: `gpt-6-astra` (released Sep 3, 2026) — do not conflate: Astra 6.2 specs must never be copied from GPT-6 Astra.
- **Context window:** no verified public spec found.
- **Modalities:** no verified public spec found.
- **Pricing (as of 2026-11-13):** no verified public price found (rumors of a ~60% price cut are unverified).
- **Architecture:** proprietary assumed; parameters unknown.

### Raw benchmarks found

- Every benchmark row reads **no verified public score found**: OpenAI has published nothing for this ID, and no leaderboard (Artificial Analysis, Epoch, BenchLM, Arena) carries a GPT-6.2 Astra entry. Community demos shared as "GPT-6.2 Astra outputs" (3D RPG one-shot builds, pelican SVG scenes) were withdrawn or clarified by their own authors as not authenticated to the model.
- Terminal-Bench 2.1 / 4.x / Tau3-Banking / GDPval-AA / Claw-Eval / Toolathon / MCP-Atlas: no verified public score found.
- GPQA Diamond / HLE / LCR / CritPt / AA Intelligence Index / Omniscience: no verified public score found.
- SWE-bench Verified / LiveCodeBench / SciCode / Vibe Code Bench / DeepSWE: no verified public score found.
- MRCR / RULER / GraphWalks: no verified public score found.

### Normalized scores (1–100)

Not computed — per `model-report-TEMPLATE.md` SELF-EXCLUSION, a folder with zero verified public benchmark numbers must not carry a scored report; placeholder scores would corrupt the average. Saved as `.md.excluded` (notes only; scores inside are ignored by `pnpm sync`). If OpenAI announces GPT-6.2 Astra with published benchmarks, this file can be replaced by a fresh scored report.

